Onboarding had Acquisition (Customer/Prospect, Cart) + Catalog pointer + Identity; Selfcare had Customer, Catalog, Portability, Billing nested, etc. — code-shaped and theme-divorced.
User guidance to include in this mistake:
(1) Think BCs two ways: frequency/distinction of lifecycle change (Customer identity/address/metadata change rarely; Subscription changes when customer does something different — more frequent; Catalog/Product different cadence again).
(2) Many apps: product, transaction to purchase product, who is purchasing.
(3) Do not invent separate domains just because Onboarding and Selfcare are separate site parts — find onboarded vs not-onboarded state and keep that in Customer domain.
(4) Target BCs for now: Customer, Catalog, Subscription — one consolidated DDD section, not per-theme DDD.